---
export const title = 'Size, pulse and dot only';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>size</code> is <code>sm</code> (the default), <code>md</code> or <code>lg</code>.
  <code>pulse</code> animates the dot for a live or in-progress state, such as "Syncing" or
  "Recording"; the animation is off when the person asks for reduced motion.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem;'>
    <wc-status-indicator intent='success' label='Small'></wc-status-indicator>
    <wc-status-indicator intent='success' label='Medium' size='md'></wc-status-indicator>
    <wc-status-indicator intent='success' label='Large' size='lg'></wc-status-indicator>
    <wc-status-indicator intent='danger' label='Recording' size='md' pulse></wc-status-indicator>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  <code>dot-only</code> hides the label where there is no room, such as a dense table column. The
  label is still read by screen readers and shows as a tooltip, so always give one. An empty
  <code>label</code> does not mean dot only: the label is what the indicator says.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-status-indicator intent='success' label='Online' dot-only></wc-status-indicator>
    <wc-status-indicator intent='warning' label='Away' dot-only></wc-status-indicator>
    <wc-status-indicator label='Offline' dot-only></wc-status-indicator>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Live status</h3>
<p>
  By default the indicator is plain text, read where it stands. Set <code>live</code> when the
  status changes while the person is on the page and the change should be announced: it gets
  <code>role="status"</code>, a polite live region. Do not set it on many indicators at once,
  such as every row of a table, or the announcements pile up.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-status-indicator id='status-indicator-live' intent='info' label='Syncing' pulse live></wc-status-indicator>
    <wc-button id='status-indicator-toggle' variant='outlined'>Finish sync</wc-button>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#status-indicator-toggle').addEventListener('click', function () {
      var el = document.querySelector('#status-indicator-live');
      var syncing = el.label === 'Syncing';
      el.label = syncing ? 'Synced' : 'Syncing';
      el.intent = syncing ? 'success' : 'info';
      el.pulse = !syncing;
      this.textContent = syncing ? 'Start sync' : 'Finish sync';
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
